x our  broken system that's been broken by 12  years of conservative incompetence and I  think the conversation about the ID  cards is a conversation for another day  are you saying that there's still a good  idea though aren't you talk to me about  um the Autumn statement the longest  serving Health secretary that we've  known in modern times of course was  Jeremy Hunt who is now the chancellor  um do you think he will look favorably  on trying to salvage what's left of our  poor Health Service  well we certainly hope so  um we understand that spending on the  NHS will be protected of course spending  has to go with reform  um but what you fundamentally have is uh  you need to have an NHS which is  underpinned by a strong economy and  after 12 years of Tory failure and then  12 weeks of complete chaos with the  disastrous mini budget uh people have  just lost confidence in the government's  ability to manage the economy and so  they're boxed in now they're either  looking at these tax increases or yet  more austerity and public spending cuts  those decisions those choices are  fundamentally because they have failed  to manage our economy and they have  crashed it in the last few months with  um well I mean reports saying that that  mini budget cost the British taxpayer 30  billion pounds it is absolutely  extraordinary so the NHS is not safe in  their hands the British economy is not  safe in their hands that's actually why  we need a general election because we  have a prime minister that doesn't have  a mandate and they have failed to give  the British people the confidence and  the trust that we need to have in our  economy moving forward that means a  proper long-term growth plan it means  Fair taxation it means closing loopholes  it means stopping non-dom status it  means removing the all of the loopholes  for the big multinational so labor  putting forward a fair taxation uh plan  and you have to win the general election  before that we certainly do do you th